  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.1-preview.32\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.32 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.31\n- First published release of this package.\n- Adds reCAPTCHA v3 and reCAPTCHA Enterprise providers with explicit provider selection and a public site key, using `IJSRuntime`. Works across all Blazor hosting models (WebAssembly, Server, Hybrid, and Auto).\n- Adds IndexedDB standard-token persistence keyed by Firebase App ID; limited-use tokens are never persisted.\n- `UseBlazor()` preserves the core debug/custom provider as the default. Selecting a reCAPTCHA provider while a core provider is configured is a composition error, as is a reCAPTCHA selection without a site key.\n- Call `IFirebaseAppCheck.EnsureReadyAsync()` before the first token read so the persisted store has settled.\n- Storage failures surface as `BlazorFirebaseAppCheckException` with `StorageGetFailure`, `StorageSetFailure`, or `StorageDeleteFailure`; there is no in-memory fallback that could hide them.",
